cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use splitplot-designer in research or a trial protocol, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "splitplot-designer: reproducible split-plot design, validation and power analysis"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/uppercrusteve/splitplot-designer"
url: "https://github.com/uppercrusteve/splitplot-designer"
authors:
  - name: "uppercrusteve"
    email: uppercrusteve@users.noreply.github.com
abstract: >-
  A Python command line tool for randomized complete block split-plot field
  trials. It validates treatment structure, geometry and replication, performs
  seed-reproducible randomization with a SHA-256 allocation digest, renders
  PNG/SVG field maps, emits correctly stratified statsmodels and R formulas,
  drafts bilingual methods text, and simulates power with whole-plot and
  residual error kept separate.
keywords:
  - split-plot
  - experimental design
  - randomization
  - power analysis
  - agronomy
  - reproducibility
